  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock id="f-5" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="f-6" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;6. During the first quarter 2026, Alabama Power Company (&#8220;respondent&#8221;) issued commercial paper and/or short-term notes to banks from time to time, with the maximum amount of such commercial paper and short-term notes outstanding at any one time of $75 million. The incurring of these obligations was authorized by the Alabama Public Service Commission (&#8220;APSC&#8221;), Informal Docket No. 5451.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="f-7" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;7. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="f-8" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;8. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="f-9" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9. See Notes to financial statements, p. 123: Note C &#8211; CONTINGENCIES &#8220;Environmental Matters&#8221; for information concerning contingencies impacting Alabama Power.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Barry and Gadsden Ash Ponds&lt;br/&gt;Air Quality &#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;Water Quality &lt;br/&gt;Coal Combustion Residuals&lt;br/&gt;Greenhouse Gases &lt;br/&gt;Nuclear Fuel Disposal Costs&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;See Notes to financial statements, p. 123: Note M &#8211; &#8220;Subsequent Events&#8221; for information concerning contingencies impacting Alabama Power.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Barry Ash Ponds&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock id="f-10" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;10. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantChangesRelatedToRespondentCompanyAppearingInAnnualReportToStockholdersTextBlock id="f-11" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;12. None.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantChangesRelatedToRespondentCompanyAppearingInAnnualReportToStockholdersTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="f-12" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;13. On March 13, 2026, Adam Ricks resigned as Assistant Comptroller.&lt;br/&gt;On March 14, 2026, Stuart Griffin was elected Assistant Comptroller.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
