lign:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;K&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:1.5pt;margin-top:2.65pt;padding-left:0.02pt;padding-right:0.02pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;&lt;a style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline" href="#ibffd4998dec94728aa89f2dbac595fa4_1293"&gt;Acquisitions and Dispositions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1.01pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;L&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:1.5pt;margin-top:2.65pt;padding-left:0.02pt;padding-right:0.02pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;&lt;a style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline" href="#ibffd4998dec94728aa89f2dbac595fa4_1299"&gt;Segment and Related Information&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1.01pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#cceeff;color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;M&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 1.02pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#cceeff;color:#0e32e1;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;Subsequent Events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:9pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;Important Note&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:9pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The following unaudited notes to the financial statements are the Combined Notes to the Financial Statements for Southern Company and its subsidiary companies (including Alabama Power) as filed in the Quarterly Report on Form 10-Q for the period ended March 31, 2026. Information contained herein relating to any individual registrant is filed by such registrant on its own behalf and each registrant makes no representation as to information related to the other registrants. The notes applicable to Alabama Power are Notes A through D, Notes F through J, and Note L. Notes E and K are not applicable to Alabama Power. In addition, the information contained in Notes A through D, Notes F through J, and Note L that relates solely to the other registrants is not applicable to Alabama Power and may not reflect any updates and in some cases, reference is made to the related SEC filing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;(A) INTRODUCTION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;These financial statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&#8220;FERC&#8221;) as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States (&#8220;GAAP&#8221;). These requirements as they relate to the financial statements differ from GAAP primarily in 1) the classification of the components of accumulated deferred income taxes, uncertain tax positions, certain miscellaneous current and accrued liabilities, prepaid assets, pension and post-retirement benefit obligations, maturities of long-term debt, asset retirement obligations, deferred debits, and deferred credits, certain regulatory assets and liabilities, 2) the presentation of majority-owned subsidiaries, certain other investments, and dividends on preferred and preference stock, 3) comparative presentation, 4) the classification of other cost of removal obligations, 5) the presentation of under recovered regulatory clauses, 6) the presentation of post-retirement defined benefit plans and unamortized debt expense, 7) the presentation of taxes applicable to Other Income and Deductions, 8) the presentation of revenues and expenses related to ASC 606, Revenue from Contracts with Customers, 9) the presentation of the fair value amounts of derivative assets and liabilities, 10) the presentation of ASU 2017-07 Compensation - Retirement Benefits (Topic 715): Improving the Presentation of Net Periodic Pension Cost and Net Periodic Postretirement Benefit Cost, 11) the presentation of ASU 2016-02, Lease (Topic 842), 12) the presentation of ASU 2018-15, Intangibles &#8211; Goodwill and Other &#8211; Internal Use Software (Topic 350), 13) the presentation of temporary cash investments greater than 90 days, and 14) the presentation of ASC 980-360-35, Public Utilities, Property, Plant and Equipment, Amount of Loss (Recovery) on Plant Abandonment. The Notes to the Financial Statements have been prepared in conformity with GAAP, except where noted. Accordingly, certain footnotes are not prepared on the same basis as the financial statements presented herein.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;Management has evaluated the impact of events occurring after March 31, 2026 up to April 29, 2026, the date that Alabama Power Company&#8217;s GAAP financial statements were issued and has updated such evaluation for disclosure purposes through May 27, 2026. These financial statements include all necessary adjustments and disclosures from these evaluations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The condensed quarterly financial statements of each Registrant included herein have been prepared by such Registrant, without audit, pursuant to the rules and regulations of the SEC. The Condensed Balance Sheets at December 31, 2025 have been derived from the audited financial statements of each Registrant. In the opinion of each Registrant's management, the information regarding such Registrant furnished herein reflects all adjustments, which, except as otherwise disclosed, are of a normal recurring nature, necessary to present fairly the results of operations for the periods ended March&#160;31, 2026 and 2025. Certain information and disclosures normally included in annual financial statements prepared in accordance with GAAP have been condensed or omitted pursuant to such rules and regulations, although each Registrant believes that the disclosures regarding such Registrant are adequate to make the information presented not misleading. Disclosures which would substantially duplicate the disclosures in the Form 1 and details which have not changed significantly in amount or composition since the filing of the Form 1 are generally omitted from this Quarterly Report on Form 3Q unless specifically required by GAAP. Therefore, these Condensed Financial Statements should be read in conjunction with the financial statements and the notes thereto included in the Form 1. Due to the seasonal variations in the demand for energy and other factors, operating results for the periods presented are not necessarily indicative of the operating results to be expected for the full year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;The preparation of financial statements in conformity with GAAP requires the use of estimates, and the actual results may differ from those estimates. Certain prior year data presented in the financial statements have been reclassified to conform to the current year presentation. These reclassifications had no impact on the overall results of operations, financial position, or cash flows of any Registrant.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:9pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;Goodwill and Other Intangible Assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;Goodwill at both March&#160;31, 2026 and December 31, 2025 was as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:76.531%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:21.269%"/&gt;&lt;td style=